   "source": [
    "# Quantitative Trading: Stochastic Volatility & Option Pricing\n",
    "## Heston Model with FFT Calibration (Carr-Madan)\n",
    "\n",
    "## 1. THEORY: Heston Model\n",
    "\n",
    "The **Heston** (1993) model prices European options when volatility is **stochastic** (changes over time), unlike Black-Scholes.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Model Dynamics\n",
    "$$dS_t = \\mu S_t dt + \\sqrt{v_t} S_t dW_t^S$$\n",
    "$$dv_t = \\kappa(\\theta - v_t) dt + \\sigma_v \\sqrt{v_t} dW_t^v$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Where:\n",
    "- $S_t$ = stock price\n",
    "- $v_t$ = instantaneous variance (latent, unobserved)\n",
    "- $\\kappa$ = mean-reversion speed (how fast vol returns to $\\theta$)\n",
    "- $\\theta$ = long-run variance level\n",
    "- $\\sigma_v$ = volatility of volatility\n",
    "- $\\rho$ = correlation between stock and volatility shocks\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why Heston?\n",
    "1. **More realistic**: Matches observed volatility smile (IV varies by strike)\n",
    "2. **Manageable**: Semi-closed-form solution via characteristic functions\n",
    "3. **Market standard**: Used widely in equity derivatives trading\n"   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "from scipy.integrate import quad, quad_vec\n",
    "from scipy.optimize import minimize, differential_evolution\n",
    "from scipy.fft import fft, fftfreq\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "from scipy import special\n",
    "\n",
    "np.random.seed(42)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Suppress warnings\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "warnings.filterwarnings('ignore')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. HESTON OPTION PRICING\n",
    "\n",
    "### 2.1 Characteristic Function Approach\n",
    "\n",
    "Heston derives a semi-closed-form solution using the **characteristic function** of log-returns.\n",
    "\n",
    "The European call price is:\n",
    "$$C(K, T) = S_0 P_1 - e^{-rT} K P_2$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where $P_j$ are probabilities computed from characteristic functions.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Numerical implementation** uses **Fourier inversion** (Carr-Madan, 1999):\n",
    "\n",
    "$$C(K, T) = \\frac{e^{-rT}}{\\pi} \\int_0^{\\infty} e^{-i\\xi \\ln K} \\frac{\\phi(\\xi - i/2)}{\\xi^2 + 1/4} d\\xi$$\n",
    "\n",
    "where $\\phi(u)$ is the characteristic function of $\\ln S_T$.\n"   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class HestonPricer:\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    Heston stochastic volatility option pricer.\n",
    "    \n",
    "    Parameters:\n",
    "    - S0: spot price\n",
    "    - r: risk-free rate\n",
    "    - T: time to maturity\n",
    "    - kappa: mean-reversion speed\n",
    "    - theta: long-run variance\n",
    "    - sigma_v: volatility of volatility\n",
    "    - rho: correlation (stock-vol)\n",
    "    - v0: current variance\n",
    "    \"\"\"\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def __init__(self, S0=100, r=0.05, kappa=2.0, theta=0.04, \n",
    "                 sigma_v=0.3, rho=-0.7, v0=0.04):\n",
    "        self.S0 = S0\n",
    "        self.r = r\n",
    "        self.kappa = kappa\n",
    "        self.theta = theta\n",
    "        self.sigma_v = sigma_v\n",
    "        self.rho = rho\n",
    "        self.v0 = v0\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def characteristic_function(self, u, T):\n",
    "        \"\"\"\n",
    "        Compute characteristic function φ(u) for log-returns under Heston.\n",
    "        This is the analytic formula from Heston's paper.\n",
    "        \"\"\"\n",
    "        a = self.kappa * self.theta\n",
    "        b = self.kappa + self.sigma_v * u * self.rho * 1j\n",
    "        c = 0.5 * self.sigma_v ** 2\n",
    "        d = np.sqrt(b**2 + c * u * (1j + u))\n",
    "        g = (b - d) / (b + d)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        exp_part = np.exp(1j * u * np.log(self.S0) + 1j * u * self.r * T)\n",
    "        exp_part *= np.exp((a / (c * (1 - g * np.exp(-d * T)))) * \n",
    "                          (self.kappa + self.sigma_v * u * self.rho * 1j - d))\n",
    "        exp_part *= np.exp((a * T) / (self.sigma_v**2))\n",
    "        exp_part *= (1 - g * np.exp(-d * T)) / (1 - g) ** (a / c)\n",
    "        exp_part *= np.exp(1j * u * self.v0 / (self.sigma_v) * \n",
    "                          (1 - np.exp(-d * T)) / (1 - g * np.exp(-d * T)))\n",
    "        \n",
    "        return exp_part\n",
    "    \n",
    "    def call_price_fft(self, K, T, N=4096):\n",
    "        \"\"\"\n",
    "        Price European call using FFT (Carr-Madan approach).\n",
    "        Much faster than numerical integration for multiple strikes.\n",
    "        \n",
    "        C(K) = exp(-r*T)/π * ∫ e^(-iξ ln K) φ(ξ - i/2) / (ξ^2 + 1/4) dξ\n",
    "        \"\"\"\n",
    "        # FFT parameters\n",
    "        dx = 2 * np.pi / N  # strike spacing in log space\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Compute characteristic function at grid points\n",
    "        xi = np.arange(N) * dx\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Evaluate characteristic function\n",
    "        cf = self.characteristic_function(xi - 0.5j, T)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Carr-Madan formula integrand\n",
    "        integrand = np.exp(-self.r * T) * cf / (xi**2 + 0.25)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # FFT to get prices\n",
    "        prices_fft = np.fft.fft(integrand * dx / np.pi)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Strikes\n",
    "        strikes = np.exp(np.arange(N) * dx / N)\n",
    "        \n",
    "        # Interpolate to desired K\n",
    "        if isinstance(K, (int, float)):\n",
    "            # Single strike\n",
    "            idx = np.argmin(np.abs(strikes - K))\n",
    "            return np.real(prices_fft[idx])\n",
    "        else:\n",
    "            # Multiple strikes\n",
    "            prices = []\n",
    "            for k in K:\n",
    "                idx = np.argmin(np.abs(strikes - k))\n",
    "                prices.append(np.real(prices_fft[idx]))\n",
    "            return np.array(prices)\n    \n",
    "    def call_price_integration(self, K, T):\n",
    "        \"\"\"\n",
    "        Price European call using direct numerical integration (slower but exact).\n",
    "        \"\"\"\n",
    "        def integrand(xi):\n",
    "            cf = self.characteristic_function(xi - 0.5j, T)\n",
    "            return np.real(np.exp(-self.r * T) * cf / (xi**2 + 0.25))\n",
    "        \n",
    "        result, _ = quad(integrand, 0, np.inf)\n",
    "        return result / np.pi\n\n# Test pricing\npricing_engine = HestonPricer(S0=100, r=0.05, kappa=2.0, theta=0.04,\n",
    "                             sigma_v=0.3, rho=-0.7, v0=0.04)\n\n# Price a call option\nK = 100  # At-the-money\nT = 0.25  # 3 months\n\ncall_price = pricing_engine.call_price_fft(K, T)\nprint(f\"\\nHeston Call Option Price\")\nprint(f\"Strike: {K}, Spot: {pricing_engine.S0}, Time to maturity: {T} years\")\nprint(f\"Call Price: ${call_price:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. VOLATILITY SMILE & CALIBRATION\n",
    "\n",
    "### 3.1 Generate Volatility Smile"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Generate option prices across strikes\nstrikes = np.linspace(80, 120, 21)\nmaturity = 0.25  # 3 months\n\nheston_prices = []\nfor K in strikes:\n",
    "    price = pricing_engine.call_price_fft(K, maturity)\n",
    "    heston_prices.append(price)\n\nheston_prices = np.array(heston_prices)\n\n# Compute implied volatility (using Black-Scholes inverse)\nfrom scipy.stats import norm\n\ndef black_scholes_call(S, K, r, T, sigma):\n",
    "    d1 = (np.log(S/K) + (r + 0.5*sigma**2)*T) / (sigma*np.sqrt(T))\n",
    "    d2 = d1 - sigma*np.sqrt(T)\n",
    "    return S*norm.cdf(d1) - K*np.exp(-r*T)*norm.cdf(d2)\n\ndef implied_vol(S, K, r, T, C_market):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Compute implied volatility using bisection.\"\"\"\n",
    "    def objective(sigma):\n",
    "        return black_scholes_call(S, K, r, T, sigma) - C_market\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Use bounding\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        from scipy.optimize import brentq\n",
    "        iv = brentq(objective, 0.001, 3.0)\n",
    "    except:\n",
    "        iv = 0.2  # fallback\n",
    "    return iv\n\nimplied_vols = []\nfor K, price in zip(strikes, heston_prices):\n",
    "    iv = implied_vol(pricing_engine.S0, K, pricing_engine.r, maturity, price)\n",
    "    implied_vols.append(iv)\n\nimplied_vols = np.array(implied_vols)\n\nprint(f\"\\nVOLATILITY SMILE\")\nprint(f\"Strike\\t\\tHeston Price\\tImplied Vol\")\nprint(\"=\"*50)\nfor k, price, iv in list(zip(strikes, heston_prices, implied_vols))[::4]:\n",
    "    print(f\"{k:.1f}\\t\\t${price:.4f}\\t\\t{iv:.4f}\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3.2 Visualize Volatility Smile"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(14, 10))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 1: Call Prices across strikes\n",
    "ax = axes[0, 0]\nax.plot(strikes, heston_prices, 'o-', linewidth=2, markersize=8, color='steelblue')\nax.set_xlabel('Strike Price', fontsize=11)\nax.set_ylabel('Call Option Price ($)', fontsize=11)\nax.set_title('Heston Model: Option Prices Across Strikes', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\nax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\nax.axvline(x=pricing_engine.S0, color='red', linestyle='--', linewidth=2, alpha=0.5, label=f'ATM (S={pricing_engine.S0})')\nax.legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 2: Volatility Smile\n",
    "ax = axes[0, 1]\nax.plot(strikes, implied_vols * 100, 'o-', linewidth=2, markersize=8, color='darkgreen')\nax.set_xlabel('Strike Price', fontsize=11)\nax.set_ylabel('Implied Volatility (%)', fontsize=11)\nax.set_title('Volatility Smile: IV vs Strike', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\nax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\nax.axvline(x=pricing_engine.S0, color='red', linestyle='--', linewidth=2, alpha=0.5)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 3: Moneyness vs IV\n",
    "ax = axes[1, 0]\nmoneyness = strikes / pricing_engine.S0\nax.plot(moneyness, implied_vols * 100, 'o-', linewidth=2, markersize=8, color='purple')\nax.axvline(x=1.0, color='red', linestyle='--', linewidth=2, alpha=0.5, label='ATM')\nax.set_xlabel('Moneyness (K/S)', fontsize=11)\nax.set_ylabel('Implied Volatility (%)', fontsize=11)\nax.set_title('The Volatility Smile: Smile Shape from Stochastic Vol', fontsize=12, fontweight='bold')\nax.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\nax.legend()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Plot 4: Heston Parameters visualization\n",
    "ax = axes[1, 1]\nparams_text = f\"\"\"\n    HESTON MODEL PARAMETERS\n    \n    Spot Price (S₀):        ${pricing_engine.S0:.2f}\n    Risk-Free Rate (r):      {pricing_engine.r:.2%}\n    Current Variance (v₀):   {pricing_engine.v0:.4f}\n    \n    Mean Reversion Speed (κ):    {pricing_engine.kappa:.2f}\n    Long-Run Variance (θ):       {pricing_engine.theta:.4f}\n    Vol of Vol (σᵥ):             {pricing_engine.sigma_v:.4f}\n    Stock-Vol Correlation (ρ):   {pricing_engine.rho:.4f}\n    \n    This negative correlation creates\n    the characteristic smile/skew:\n    Out-of-money puts are more expensive\n    than Black-Scholes predicts.\n\"\"\"\nax.text(0.05, 0.95, params_text, transform=ax.transAxes, fontsize=11,\n        verticalalignment='top', family='monospace',\n        bbox=dict(boxstyle='round', facecolor='wheat', alpha=0.5))\nax.axis('off')\n",
    "\nplt.tight_layout()\nplt.savefig('heston_volatility_smile.png', dpi=150, bbox_inches='tight')\nplt.show()"
   ]
  },
